This license covers grāmatr's own code in this repository — the Docker
Compose definition, documentation, and any scripts added here directly.
It does NOT cover the three guards this stack composes, each of which
is its own project with its own license and (for injection-guard) its
own third-party model obligations:

- gramatr/secret-guard — MIT (gitleaks, the engine it wraps, is also MIT)
- gramatr/pii-guard — MIT (Presidio and its default spaCy model, both MIT)
- gramatr/injection-guard — MIT for its own code; the model it loads at
  runtime (Meta's Llama Prompt Guard 2) is separately licensed under
  the Llama 4 Community License — see NOTICE.md and that repo's own
  NOTICE/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/ for the authoritative terms.

See NOTICE.md in this repository for a summary of what that means for
anyone running this stack.
